From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:08:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] notifications: sound, vibration and LED through feedbackd, charging LED
Description:
 The shell gave no feedback for notifications: nothing vibrated and the
 LED stayed dark, only applications that play their own sound were
 heard.
 .
 The notification popup provider now triggers a feedbackd event for
 every new notification with normal or critical urgency, chosen by its
 category: incoming calls and alarms (call.incoming, x-kde.incoming-call,
 alarm.ringing) last as long as their notification, cell broadcasts,
 instant messages and emails get their own events, everything else the
 generic one. Applications using KNotification play their own sounds,
 their events get no sound from feedbackd (profile quiet). In do not
 disturb mode only alarms and the applications allowed to show popups
 keep their feedback; the others only light the LED. Notifications the
 user hid from popups and the drawer give no feedback.
 .
 A notification arriving while the phone is locked or the display is
 off starts a reminder on the LED until it is seen: unlock, display on
 without a lock, or the action drawer opening; closing all those
 notifications ends it as well. While the battery charges the LED shows
 the battery-charging event. Which event a device shows when they
 compete is up to the priorities of the feedbackd theme.
 .
 A new notification turns the display on (PowerDevil wakeup), except in
 do not disturb mode; new setting in the shell settings, on by default.
Author: masterxq <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: no
License: GPL-2.0-or-later, LGPL-2.0-or-later (as the patched files)
Last-Update: 2026-11-28
